perties from personally observed or model-derived evidence. Explain an implemented hardness check using its actual threshold and resolved material value, without inventing a hardness measurement; if personal contact inspection is separately required, identify that requirement and its existing executable inspection route and cost. Do not silently introduce a new inspection prerequisite. Use represented sheet geometry and shared support/collision state, not terrain labels alone; absent required evidence stays unknown. Missing food must not invalidate surface assessment, although food remains required for preparation. Retain bounded dated results with source identities and geometry revisions; later preparation revalidates mutable conditions. Old suitable-only records migrate as legacy results with unavailable diagnostics explicitly unknown; never reconstruct past failures from present state. Execution is atomic at the paid round boundary: validate actor alive and sufficient energy, evaluate current state, debit once and emit root-surface-assessed. Before commitment, interruption or death cancels with no debit or result; there is no escrow, reserved material, persistent work or automatic continuation. Return actual remaining work of one round before commitment and zero after completion. Invalid identity or authorization errors emit failed without disclosing inaccessible state. Subscribe and render root-surface-assessed and failed; optionally emit information-confirmed only for a genuinely new, evidence-supported finding under the existing qualification rules. Add no physical objects, stock, mastery or changes to protected mental accounts. Implementation and review consume no simulation time.\",\n      \"experienceReview\": \"Explanation alone, registration and learning receive no feedback. A paid assessment that successfully establishes genuinely new, personally applicable information may use the existing grounded-understanding source through information-confirmed on root-preparation-surface, qualified=true, with the assessor as sole beneficiary: amount 0.8, cap 1, duration 8 rounds, refresh repetition and cooldown 12 rounds. Its existing maintained component gains 0.035 per qualifying event and decays 0.0015 per round without continued qualifying participation. Repeated known diagnostics do not qualify; no additional practice or alias source is created. Nutrition, health and physical comfort are unchanged.\",\n      \"visualReview\": \"Bind the paid root-surface-assessed event to a dated checklist showing pass, fail and unknown separately, actual values versus thresholds, evidence references and explicit model assumptions. Display the existing sheet footprint and required rectangle at the assessed site using shared geometry, with support or collision failures marked only where actually resolved. Replay stores the assessment-time result and geometry references rather than substituting current conditions. Failed or unresolved checks must remain visible even when another check fails; presentation must not depict food processing, consumed materials or a suitable surface unless those effects actually occurred.\",\n      \"learning\": 1\n    }\n  ]\n}","logprobs":[]}

